    "9c80a871-bf8f-4cdf-b324-980b4ca11d93": {
      "id": "9c80a871-bf8f-4cdf-b324-980b4ca11d93",
      "message": {
        "author": {
          "name": null,
          "role": "assistant"
        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Here is a **simple, military-style calisthenics calendar** designed for **15\u201320 minutes per day**, no equipment, very disciplined, and sustainable. This mirrors classic military PT: push, pull, hinge, squat, core, conditioning, with built-in recovery.\n\nYou can print this, screenshot it, or drop it into a planner.\n\n\ue200image_group\ue202{\"query\":[\"military calisthenics workout\",\"push ups exercise\",\"bodyweight squats exercise\",\"plank core exercise\",\"jumping jacks exercise\"]}\ue201\n\n---\n\n## DAILY STRUCTURE (15\u201320 MIN TOTAL)\n\n**1. Warm-Up (3 minutes)**  \nEvery day, no exceptions  \n- Jumping jacks x 30  \n- Arm circles x 20  \n- Hip circles x 20  \n- High knees x 30 seconds  \n- Air squats x 15  \n\n---\n\n## WEEKLY CALENDAR (REPEAT FOR 4\u20136 WEEKS)\n\n### **MONDAY \u2013 UPPER BODY PUSH**\n15\u201320 min total  \n- Push-ups: 4 x max reps (stop 1\u20132 reps before failure)  \n- Shoulder taps: 3 x 20  \n- Pike push-ups: 3 x 10  \n- Plank hold: 2 x 45\u201360 sec  \n\nOptional finisher (2 min):  \n- Push-ups EMOM (every minute on the minute) x 2 min\n\n---\n\n### **TUESDAY \u2013 LOWER BODY**\n- Bodyweight squats: 4 x 25  \n- Reverse lunges: 3 x 10 each leg  \n- Wall sit: 2 x 60 sec  \n- Calf raises: 3 x 30  \n\nOptional finisher:  \n- Squat hold x 90 seconds\n\n---\n\n### **WEDNESDAY \u2013 CORE + CARDIO**\n- Sit-ups or crunches: 3 x 25  \n- Leg raises: 3 x 12\u201315  \n- Plank: 3 x 45 sec  \n- Mountain climbers: 3 x 40 sec  \n\nOptional finisher:  \n- 2 minutes nonstop mountain climbers\n\n---\n\n### **THURSDAY \u2013 UPPER BODY PULL + STABILITY**\n(No equipment version)  \n- Superman holds: 3 x 30 sec  \n- Reverse snow angels (lying face down): 3 x 15  \n- Towel rows (door-anchored or floor slide): 3 x 12  \n- Side plank: 2 x 30 sec each side  \n\nOptional finisher:  \n- Hollow body hold x 60 sec\n\n---\n\n### **FRIDAY \u2013 FULL BODY CONDITIONING**\nCircuit x 3 rounds (no rest between exercises)  \n- Push-ups x 15  \n- Squats x 20  \n- Sit-ups x 20  \n- Jumping jacks x 40  \nRest 60 sec between rounds  \n\nOptional finisher:  \n- Burpees x 10\u201315\n\n---\n\n### **SATURDAY \u2013 ACTIVE RECOVERY / MOBILITY**\n- Slow air squats x 20  \n- Walking lunges x 10 each leg  \n- Shoulder mobility (circles, swings) x 2 min  \n- Long plank x 2 min (break if needed)  \n\nGoal: blood flow, not exhaustion\n\n---\n\n### **SUNDAY \u2013 REST**\nNo training.  \nLight walk or stretch only.\n\n---\n\n## PROGRESSION (VERY MILITARY, VERY SIMPLE)\nEach week, **add ONE of the following**:\n- +5 push-ups per workout  \n- +10 squats per workout  \n- +15 seconds to planks  \n- +1 round to circuits  \n\nNo ego. Perfect form. Consistency beats intensity.\n\n---\n\n## RULES (MILITARY MINDSET)\n- Same time every day  \n- No phone during workout  \n- Finish even when motivation is gone  \n- Missed day = make it up next day  \n\nIf you want, I can:\n- Convert this into a **printable PDF**\n- Customize for **women-focused strength**\n- Add a **fat-loss or endurance version**\n- Build a **30-, 60-, or 90-day progression**\n\nJust tell me."
          ]
